        "date": "2026-11-12T02:31:23Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): judge the index swing of any work-turning rotary about a level line\n\nThe index-swing clause (#804, #813) judged only an A about X. A table B\n(stated [0,1,0], or unstated and named B) and an A stated level but off\nX read \"off X\" and indexed unjudged. rotary_line now returns the line\nitself: Horizontal(unit u) is judged like the microARC A - the tip at\nthe safe Z (nose_to_axis - tool length) against the farthest turning\nvertex from the line through the WCS origin, |(p - o) x u| - with the\nsame refusal for an unstated nose_to_axis; Vertical (a C) stays safe and\nunjudged; a leaning, zero or non-finite vector refuses by name (\"not\njudged\"); no vector and no RS-274 letter still refuses (#813). Two\nrotaries turning the work take the sweep from the WCS origin, since each\nmoves the other's line. A non-finite vertex sweeps without bound\n(refused). The pre-#804 load note now names every non-vertical rotary.\n\nPinned by the new index_swing_horizontal suite over a test-only table-B\nmachine file; decision in docs/decisions/818-swing-any-horizontal.md.\n\nFixes #818\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
